  "question": {
    "text": "Let from a point <math><mi>A</mi><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>,</mo><mi></mi><mi>k</mi></mrow></mfenced></math> chords of contact are drawn to the ellipse <math><msup><mrow><mi>x</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><msup><mrow><mi>y</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>6</mn></math> where all these chords touch the ellipse <math><msup><mrow><mi>x</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo>+</mo><mn>4</mn><msup><mrow><mi>y</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn></math>.&nbsp;Then, the perimeter (in units) of the locus of point <math><mi>A</mi></math> is"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "<math><mn>2</mn><mi>π</mi></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "<math><mn>3</mn><mi>π</mi></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "<math><mn>4</mn><mi>π</mi></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "<math><mn>6</mn><mi>π</mi></math>",
      "is_correct": true
    }
  ],
  "correct_answer": [
    "D"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>Let the chord of contact is <math><mi>P</mi><mi>Q</mi></math> which touches <math><msup><mrow><mi>x</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo>+</mo><mn>4</mn><msup><mrow><mi>y</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn></math> at <math><mi>R</mi></math><br />Now, assume <math><mi>R</mi><mo>=</mo><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mn>2</mn><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">cos</mi></mrow><mo>&#8289;</mo><mrow><mi>&#952;</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">sin</mi></mrow><mo>&#8289;</mo><mrow><mi>&#952;</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mfenced></math><br />Equation of the chord of contact&nbsp;<math><mi>P</mi><mi>Q</mi></math> is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>h</mi><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>y</mi><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>6</mn><mo>&#8230;</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">i</mi></mfenced></math><br />Again, the equation of the tangent&nbsp;<math><mi>P</mi><mi>Q</mi></math> is <math><mfrac><mrow><mi>x</mi><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">cos</mi></mrow><mo>&#8289;</mo><mrow><mi>&#952;</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>y</mi><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">sin</mi></mrow><mo>&#8289;</mo><mrow><mi>&#952;</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mi></mi><mo>&#8230;</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">i</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">i</mi></mrow></mfenced></math><br />From <math><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">i</mi></mrow></mfenced></math> and <math><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">i</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">i</mi></mrow></mfenced></math>, we get,</p><p>&nbsp;<math><mfrac><mrow><mi>h</mi><mn>2</mn></mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">cos</mi></mrow><mo>&#8289;</mo><mrow><mi>&#952;</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>k</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>s</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>n</mi><mi>&#952;</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>6</mn></math><br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>cos</mi><mo>&#8289;</mo><mi>&#952;</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mi>h</mi><mn>3</mn></mfrac><mo>,</mo><mi>sin</mi><mo>&#8289;</mo><mi>&#952;</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mi>k</mi><mn>3</mn></mfrac><mspace linebreak=\"newline\"/><mo>&#8658;</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>9</mn></math></p><p>Hence, the perimeter of the circle is&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>6</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#960;</mi></math>&nbsp;units</p>"
  }
}